INTERPRETATION

The four-stage learned-U transfer independently reproduced on a completely fresh ten-world confirmation set.

The same frozen 25-percent learned U-recruitment authority caused real developmental recruitment differences without retraining, authority increase, task identity, stage identity, global queue information, evaluator correctness, or future information.

Nine exact-parent worlds satisfied the baseline contract, clearing the preregistered coverage requirement, and every eligible learned-vs-parent pair preserved the full functional envelope.

This independently confirms the Task-4 transfer result.

BOUNDARY

Do not increase alpha.
Do not grant learned C/S authority.
Do not add online adaptation.
Do not add recursive self-modification.

NEXT SCIENTIFIC DIRECTION

Sequential depth through four stages is now independently supported.

The next task-distance experiment should change compositional structure rather than simply append a fifth sequential stage.

The broader Yggdrasil North Star is now a capable general-purpose language model on consumer hardware using developmental/cellular computation.

The accepted Task-4 confirmation is the shared scientific baseline for three isolated research lanes:

YGG-A:
developmental computation and structural topology.

YGG-B:
language bridge and sequence learning.

YGG-C:
efficiency, scaling, and consumer-hardware feasibility.

Cross-lane scientific changes require explicit promotion to a new shared baseline.

PLAIN-SPEAK INTERPRETATION

The four-step result repeated on fresh worlds.

The neural recruiter is not just surviving one lucky test set.

It is making real developmental decisions on a deeper compositional task while the organism keeps the same functional behavior as the hand-written parent.

That is strong enough to stop spending most of our effort on longer straight pipelines.

The next work should test different computation structure, sequence/language learning, and whether the architecture can remain efficient enough to become a practical language model.

